<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zēlo</span></b> , āre,
			v. a., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζηλόω</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To love with zeal</i> or <i>ardently</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">populum summo pietatis amore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Carm. adv. Marc. 4, 36</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Aug. Conf. 1,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To be jealous of</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non zeles mulierem sinus tui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Ecclus. 9, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>To be zealous for</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zelat zelum legis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1
					Macc. 2, 58</span></i>
			.—Also in <i>dep.</i> form: zelatus
			est legem. <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Macc. 2, 26</span></i>.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">zelatus est pro Deo suo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Num. 25, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
